{
  "$comment": "Who may call each route of the backend (issue #541; WSTG-v42-ATHZ-02, ATHZ-04; WSTG-APIT-02, APIT-04 at latest@87cf4a4). Keyed 'METHOD path' as app.openapi() names it. backend/tests/test_authorization_matrix.py fails on a route missing here (deny by default), on a stale entry, and when a call disagrees: anonymous gets 401 unless public, a role below the minimum 403, a member of another company 403 or 404, the minimum role gets past the check. 'body' and 'query' fill what the request builder cannot infer from the schema; 'allowed_status' lists a 401 or 403 the allowed caller may get for a reason that is not authorization; 'why' says why a route is public, signed or open to any signed-in caller. public_routes is the list SECURITY.md §3.2 documents; a change to it is a security decision for review.",
